<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta content='text/html; charset=UTF-8' http-equiv='Content-Type' />
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
    .container { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
    .header { background-color: #dc2626; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; }
    .content { background-color: #f9fafb; padding: 20px; }
    .alert { background-color: #fee2e2; border-left: 4px solid #dc2626; padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; }
    /* Amber, not red: nothing has gone wrong with the senior here — the call
       simply was not placed, and the alarm colour would misdirect. */
    .header.info { background-color: #b45309; }
    .alert.info { background-color: #fef3c7; border-left-color: #b45309; }
    .button { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; background-color: #dc2626; color: #ffffff !important; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 5px; margin: 10px 5px; }
    .footer { text-align: center; padding: 20px; color: #6b7280; font-size: 12px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header<%= " info" if @phone_failure %>">
      <h1><%= if @phone_failure then "☎️ Not reached" elsif @phone_calls == :no_answer then "☎️ No answer" else "⚠️ Not marked done" end %></h1>
    </div>

    <div class="content">
      <p>Hi <%= @caregiver.display_name %>,</p>

      <div class="alert<%= " info" if @phone_failure %>">
        <% if @phone_failure == :could_not_place %>
          <strong>Remindly tried to call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %> and could not get through.</strong>
        <% elsif @phone_failure %>
          <strong>Remindly did not call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %>.</strong>
        <% elsif @phone_calls == :no_answer %>
          <strong>Remindly called <%= @senior.display_name %> <%= pluralize(@calls_placed, "time") %> about <%= @reminder.title %>, and nobody answered.</strong>
        <% elsif @phone_calls == :heard %>
          <strong>Remindly's call to <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %> was answered, but nobody confirmed it.</strong>
        <% else %>
          <strong><%= @senior.display_name %> has not marked <%= @reminder.title %> as done.</strong>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <% if @scheduled_at %>
        <% if @phone_failure == :could_not_place %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>.
            <%= pluralize(@attempts, "attempt") %> made, and not one of them
            reached the phone network. That is a fault at our end.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure == :not_attempted_in_time %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>, and was closed
            as missed before Remindly managed to place the call. That is a fault at our end.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure == :added_after_its_time %>
          <%# No call was placed, so no call was ignored. This row was written
              after the time it names -- almost always because a reminder was
              added or edited to a time that had already passed today -- and
              Remindly deliberately does not telephone about a dose whose moment
              went by before the row existed. Saying so is the difference
              between explaining and accusing.

              About the call, and only the call. The screen client announces
              anything due and unacknowledged today, back-filled rows included,
              and the dashboard lists it with a Done button beside it -- so
              "she was never asked" is a sentence this email cannot honestly
              say. What it knows is that Remindly did not telephone. %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>, but it was added
            to the schedule after that time had already passed — usually because the reminder
            was added or edited today. Remindly does not call about a time that has gone by,
            so no call was placed for this one.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>, which is outside
            the hours Remindly is allowed to place reminder calls — between
            <%= @calling_hours %> in <%= @senior.display_name %>'s own time.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_calls == :no_answer %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>. Nobody pressed 1 to hear the reminder,
            so it was never spoken: the phone rang out, or a voicemail picked up.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_calls == :heard %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @due_label %>. Somebody answered and pressed 1 to hear it
            at <%= @heard_at.strftime("%-l:%M %p") %>, and nobody pressed 1 afterwards
            to say it was done.
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <p>It was due <%= @due_label %> and has not been marked done since.</p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>

      <%#
        The caveat that matters more than the one on the completed email. This
        notification says a button was not pressed, and the most likely
        explanation is that it was not pressed — but "did it and forgot to say
        so" is common enough that leading a caregiver straight to alarm, before
        they have picked up the phone, is the wrong default.
      %>
      <% if @phone_failure %>
        <%# What this email is allowed to conclude, and it is less than it used
            to claim. "Remindly did not ask" is not true of a care receiver
            whose screen announced the reminder and showed a Done button beside
            it -- which is every one of them, since both channels fire. The
            telephone is the only channel this email has evidence about. %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          Remindly did not reach <%= @senior.display_name %> by phone, so this
          says nothing about whether they did it.
        </p>
      <% elsif @phone_calls == :no_answer %>
        <%# Not the screen caveat. "They may have done it without marking it"
            is a fair reading of a skipped button and the wrong one for a
            telephone nobody answered, which for somebody living alone is the
            more urgent signal -- the old wording talked caregivers out of it. %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          This does not tell you whether they did it, only that nobody answered
          the phone. If that is unusual for <%= @senior.display_name %>, it may
          be worth checking in.
        </p>
      <% elsif @phone_calls == :heard %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          They may have done it without pressing the key, or not at all.
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          This means nobody pressed <strong>Done</strong> on their device. It does
          not necessarily mean it was not done — they may have done it without
          marking it.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin: 30px 0;">
        <a href="<%= @dashboard_url %>" class="button" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none;">View <%= @senior.display_name %>'s dashboard</a>
      </div>

      <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
        This is an automated notification from Remindly to help you keep track of <%= @senior.display_name %>'s reminders.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
      <p>Remindly - Caregiver Coordination</p>
      <p>You're receiving this because you're a caregiver for <%= @senior.display_name %>. You can turn these off in your notification settings.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
